---
// The Four Laws site's only conversion point.
//
// This site is the deeper property — sixteen pages, three tools, a glossary and
// an FAQ — and until now it captured nothing. Someone who has just read the
// Full Reference or worked through the glossary is the warmest reader either
// site will ever have, and they were leaving with nowhere to go but a nav link.
//
// It points at thejonmartin.com/#notify rather than duplicating the Netlify
// form here: the two sites are separate Netlify projects with separate form
// buckets, and one waitlist split across two buckets is worse than one link.
---

<aside class="cta-block">
	<span class="label kicker">From the author</span>
	<p class="lede">
		These laws are the vocabulary I use in the field. If you're running a
		founder-led professional services firm and something structural keeps
		breaking, I write diagnoses — not implementations.
	</p>
	<a class="cta" href="https://thejonmartin.com/#notify">
		See what that is &rarr;
	</a>
</aside>

<style>
	/* Sage left rule rather than mustard: this appears on every content page, and
	   an accent that shows up everywhere isn't an accent. Mustard stays reserved
	   for genuine per-page outliers. */
	.cta-block {
		margin: 3.5rem 0 0;
		padding: 1.5rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
		border-left: 3px solid var(--sage);
		border-radius: 4px;
	}
	.kicker {
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		color: var(--sage);
		display: block;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}
	.lede {
		margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
		font-size: 0.97rem;
	}
	.cta {
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		text-decoration: none;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
	}
	.cta:hover {
		border-bottom-color: var(--plum);
	}
</style>
